---
import Article from "../../../layouts/Article.astro";
import KeyTakeaway from "../../../components/KeyTakeaway.astro";
import InfoBox from "../../../components/InfoBox.astro";
import ComparisonTable from "../../../components/ComparisonTable.astro";
import StepList from "../../../components/StepList.astro";
import Step from "../../../components/Step.astro";
---

<Article
  title="How to Store Forest Shuffle With All Three Expansions (Sleeved)"
  description="Do Forest Shuffle and its expansions fit in one box with sleeves? Card counts, sleeve size, and how to sort all 307 cards so setup takes seconds."
  game="forest-shuffle"
  gameTitle="Forest Shuffle"
  category="Guide"
  product="forest-shuffle-insert"
  publishDate="2026-11-20"
>
  <p>
    Forest Shuffle comes with no insert, and every expansion adds another
    deck to the same box. The cards fit; keeping them findable is the problem.
    Here's how many cards you're dealing with, which sleeves to buy, and a
    sorting order that makes setup quick.
  </p>

  <KeyTakeaway answer="Everything fits in the base game box, sleeved: Lookout says so for all three expansions. With the base game, Alpine, Woodland Edge and Exploration you have 307 cards. Sleeves listed for Forest Shuffle are usually 59 × 91 mm. Store the main deck together, and keep the winter cards, caves, reference cards and Exploration's solo deck apart, because those are the ones you need separately at setup." />

  <h2>How many cards you need to sleeve</h2>

  <ComparisonTable title="Card counts">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Box</th>
          <th>Cards</th>
          <th>Running total</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Base game</td><td>180</td><td>180</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Alpine</td><td>36</td><td>216</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Woodland Edge</td><td>36</td><td>252</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Exploration</td><td>55</td><td>307</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </ComparisonTable>

  <p>
    The base game's 180 cards break down into 66 tree cards, 92 animal and
    plant cards, 3 winter cards, 5 caves and 14 reference cards.
  </p>

  <h2>Which sleeves fit</h2>
  <p>
    Retailers usually list 59 × 91 mm sleeves for Forest Shuffle. Gamegenic
    makes official Forest Shuffle art sleeves in packs of 185 (165 printed with
    the card back, 20 clear), which covers the base game. For the expansions
    you need roughly another 130.
  </p>
  <InfoBox type="info" title="Sleeves make the box tighter, not impossible">
    Lookout says the Alpine and Woodland Edge cards fit in the base box even
    sleeved, and that the whole Exploration deck still fits too. What you lose
    is the loose space that made the cards easy to grab.
  </InfoBox>

  <h2>A sorting order that makes setup quick</h2>

  <StepList title="Sort by what you need at setup, not by expansion">
    <Step number={1} title="Main deck: trees, animals and plants together">
      Expansion cards get shuffled into the base deck anyway, so there's no
      point keeping them apart. Split the main deck into a few stacks so you
      can lift it out without it fanning across the table.
    </Step>
    <Step number={2} title="Winter cards on their own">
      Only three, and they go into the deck at setup. If they're mixed in,
      you'll be hunting for them every game.
    </Step>
    <Step number={3} title="Caves">
      One per player. With Exploration, keep its caves next to the plain ones
      so choosing caves at the start is quick.
    </Step>
    <Step number={4} title="Reference cards">
      Fourteen of them in the base game. They're not part of the deck, so
      give them their own slot.
    </Step>
    <Step number={5} title="Exploration's solo deck and special cards">
      The Automa deck and challenges only come out for solo games, so give
      them their own slot.
    </Step>
    <Step number={6} title="Score pad and pencil">
      Scoring takes a while in Forest Shuffle, and the pencil is always the
      thing that's missing.
    </Step>
  </StepList>

  <h2>Our insert does exactly this</h2>
  <p>
    We designed a two-tray insert for the whole collection, sleeved, in the
    original box with the lid closed. The bottom tray holds the tree cards
    and all the animal and plant cards. The top tray holds the winter cards,
    the caves, every Exploration deck and the rest. Each slot has an embossed
    icon (tree, snowflake, cave, trophy, fox, question mark) so every deck goes
    back in the same place, finger cutouts to lift a stack in one go, and a spot
    for the pencil. At the table you lift the trays out, and setup takes seconds.
  </p>
  <p>
    New to the expansions? See
    <a href="/games/forest-shuffle/forest-shuffle-expansions/">what Alpine, Woodland Edge and Exploration add</a>.
  </p>
</Article>
